WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:18.935
walked into Grandpa's study wearing a necklace and a long dress pinned at the shoulders.

2
00:00:19.555 --> 00:00:21.176
Her hair was gathered into a net.

3
00:00:21.196 --> 00:00:23.117
"How do I look, Grandpa?

4
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:25.338
Can you guess what I am for Halloween?"

5
00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:28.139
"A woman from ancient Greece of course!"

6
00:00:28.759 --> 00:00:30.100
Grandpa said, smiling.

7
00:00:30.828 --> 00:00:33.950
"And which city-state, may I ask, are you from?"

8
00:00:35.091 --> 00:00:35.952
Laurie frowned.

9
00:00:35.972 --> 00:00:37.993
"I hadn't really thought about it.

10
00:00:38.573 --> 00:00:40.294
Sparta? Athens?"

11
00:00:41.135 --> 00:00:44.737
she answered, naming the only two old Greek cities she knew.

12
00:00:44.757 --> 00:00:48.180
"Those are two very different cities.

13
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.162
They were also enemies for many years.

14
00:00:52.342 --> 00:00:56.465
Maybe I should tell you about them so you can decide which one you'd rather live in.

15
00:00:57.886 --> 00:01:01.985
The Spartans were known for being serious, disciplined warriors.

16
00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:06.890
Every man joined the army and spent most of his life in the military.

17
00:01:08.251 --> 00:01:14.136
Training began at age seven, when boys were taken from their families and sent to live in military

18
00:01:14.216 --> 00:01:23.004
camps. They practiced sports for hours each day because having a weak body was considered dishonorable among Spartans.

19
00:01:23.805 --> 00:01:26.968
They were taught to live with only the barest necessities.

20
00:01:28.636 --> 00:01:35.199
Sometimes they were even starved on purpose so they would learn to fearlessly steal or kill their own

21
00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:36.479
food for survival.

22
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:43.602
They were also served a black soup made of pork stewed in pigs' blood, vinegar, and salt to

23
00:01:43.662 --> 00:01:44.583
make them strong.

24
00:01:45.683 --> 00:01:51.145
Besides undergoing physical training, they had to learn how to become brave warriors.

25
00:01:52.226 --> 00:01:57.048
A good Spartan warrior could never cry out in pain or surrender easily.

26
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.304
Even the Spartan women were expected to be strong and fearless.

27
00:02:03.425 --> 00:02:11.152
Unlike women in most other Greek cities, women of Sparta spent lots of time outdoors, exercising: they ran,

28
00:02:11.552 --> 00:02:13.314
did gymnastics, and danced.

29
00:02:14.315 --> 00:02:22.103
Part of a woman's duty was to provide her husband with a physically fit—preferably male—child who would become

30
00:02:22.143 --> 00:02:23.344
a strong warrior.

31
00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:29.163
In order to give birth to a healthy child, it was thought the mother must be fit and

32
00:02:29.223 --> 00:02:29.904
healthy too.

33
00:02:31.365 --> 00:02:36.288
Girls also received good educations and were allowed to own property as adults!

34
00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:41.772
This really shocked Greeks from other cities, where women weren't allowed such things.

35
00:02:42.632 --> 00:02:49.697
Spartan men and women were able to devote their lives to building a powerful Spartan military because all

36
00:02:49.757 --> 00:02:52.499
their farming and other labor was done by slaves.

37
00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.342
In fact, most of Sparta's economy ran on slave labor.

38
00:02:58.542 --> 00:03:02.465
But just because they had slaves doesn't mean Spartans were extravagant.

39
00:03:03.205 --> 00:03:05.967
They were expected to scorn wealth and luxury.

40
00:03:06.687 --> 00:03:12.050
They didn't have parties and, besides religious rites, had very few celebrations.

41
00:03:13.091 --> 00:03:15.372
They didn't wear jewelry or make much art.

42
00:03:16.293 --> 00:03:25.426
Today the word 'spartan' can describe someone who is courageous and self-disciplined, but also something that is extremely

43
00:03:25.566 --> 00:03:27.327
simple and not at all luxurious.

44
00:03:28.168 --> 00:03:30.910
What do you say, Laurie, could you be a Spartan?"

45
00:03:32.771 --> 00:03:38.115
"Hmm I could play sports, learn stuff, and eventually own my own house.

46
00:03:38.955 --> 00:03:44.599
That doesn't sound so bad, but I want to hear about Athens before I decide," Laurie said.

47
00:03:44.619 --> 00:03:46.000
"You got it.

48
00:03:46.861 --> 00:03:50.784
Athenians enjoyed a lifestyle very different from the Spartans.

49
00:03:51.644 --> 00:03:57.107
Women's main duties were to raise children, take care of the household, and weave wool.

50
00:03:58.568 --> 00:04:03.671
If you were an Athenian, you probably would have made that beautiful dress of yours at home.

51
00:04:04.691 --> 00:04:09.614
Now taking care of the household could mean different things depending on how rich you were.

52
00:04:10.374 --> 00:04:16.637
If you were well-off, you probably had many slaves who would clean, watch the children, and bake bread.

53
00:04:17.538 --> 00:04:21.080
If you weren't, well, you might be doing all that work yourself.

54
00:04:22.344 --> 00:04:28.088
Although boys began school around age seven, Athenian girls didn't get to go to school.

55
00:04:29.228 --> 00:04:35.012
Around age 13 or so, they got married and began their lives as wives and mothers.

56
00:04:35.933 --> 00:04:38.514
But Athens was a truly incredible city.

57
00:04:39.575 --> 00:04:45.578
It is often called the birthplace of democracy because it was the first city to test out democracy,

58
00:04:45.919 --> 00:04:47.620
or government run by citizens.

59
00:04:48.924 --> 00:04:56.487
Athenians held city meetings at which all citizens—meaning Greek men who were born in the city—could share their

60
00:04:56.527 --> 00:05:00.168
opinions. Then citizens were allowed to vote.

61
00:05:01.028 --> 00:05:05.530
Sometimes they decided big issues, such as whether the city should go to war.

62
00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:10.412
Their style of government developed into the democracy we know today.

63
00:05:12.388 --> 00:05:20.590
Athens was also home to the famous Acropolis, an immense complex of temples, theaters, and other impressive buildings.

64
00:05:21.651 --> 00:05:28.792
The temples were dedicated to the worship of the Greeks' many gods and goddesses, whom the Athenians respected,

65
00:05:28.972 --> 00:05:30.833
feared, and often celebrated.

66
00:05:31.873 --> 00:05:35.154
Athenians were not spartan like the Spartans.

67
00:05:36.394 --> 00:05:41.956
They enjoyed sculpture, music, theater, poetry, and philosophy.

68
00:05:43.528 --> 00:05:47.169
Maybe you've heard of the great thinkers Socrates and Aristotle?

69
00:05:47.789 --> 00:05:49.710
They were both from Athens.

70
00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:57.092
Athenian citizens were deep thinkers, but they also liked wine, feasts, and celebrations!

71
00:05:57.652 --> 00:06:05.174
Grooming was also an important part of life; both men and women took hot baths and rubbed themselves

72
00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:06.095
with olive oil.

73
00:06:07.475 --> 00:06:09.996
Women owned lots of makeup and perfume.

74
00:06:11.036 --> 00:06:16.880
Athenians wore beautiful gold jewelry, a lot of which can be seen in museums today.

75
00:06:18.341 --> 00:06:25.387
Sparta and Athens had very different ideas about how people should live and govern themselves, but each grew

76
00:06:25.427 --> 00:06:26.728
to be a strong city.

77
00:06:27.748 --> 00:06:29.470
Eventually they clashed.

78
00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:37.936
Both wanted to rule the other Greek city-states, and in 431 BC, they fought in the Peloponnesian War.

79
00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:46.403
After nearly thirty years of battle, the Spartans were victorious and the good times in Athens ended.

80
00:06:47.744 --> 00:06:50.385
So what do you think, my little Grecian?

81
00:06:50.925 --> 00:06:55.947
Which ancient city would you like to live in—Sparta or Athens?"

82
00:06:56.468 --> 00:06:57.388
Grandpa asked.

83
00:06:58.108 --> 00:06:59.649
Laurie considered her options.

84
00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:06.212
"Being a Spartan would mean I'd live a simple—and maybe harsh—life, but get to run around a lot.

85
00:07:06.828 --> 00:07:12.873
Being an Athenian would mean I'd witness the birth and development of democracy, but I wouldn't get to

86
00:07:12.913 --> 00:07:14.854
participate because I'm a girl.

87
00:07:15.455 --> 00:07:16.355
Sparta it is!"

88
00:07:18.597 --> 00:07:22.340
Laurie cried, snatching off her necklace and raising a fist in the air.

89
00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:24.221
She marched out of the study.

90
00:07:24.241 --> 00:07:27.544
"Lace up your sneakers, Mom," she called.

91
00:07:27.564 --> 00:07:33.028
"We're jogging to the Halloween parade—in true Spartan style!"
